<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Optimizer on Beyond Swift</title><link>https://beyondswift.com/tags/optimizer/</link><description>Recent content in Optimizer on Beyond Swift</description><generator>Hugo -- 0.163.3</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 02:51:00 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://beyondswift.com/tags/optimizer/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Debug and Release run different code</title><link>https://beyondswift.com/debug-vs-release-builds-what-actually-changes/</link><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 02:51:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://beyondswift.com/debug-vs-release-builds-what-actually-changes/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A crash report comes in from TestFlight. The stack points at a function that is green on every simulator run and every device debug session you can throw at it. You cannot reproduce it. The code looks correct.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-swift" data-lang="swift"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;averageLatency&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt; samples: [Int]) -&amp;gt; Int {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; assert(&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;samples.isEmpty, &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;never call this with no samples&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; samples.reduce(&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;) &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; samples.count &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// crashes in Release, not Debug&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Read it and answer: why does this survive every debug run and divide by zero in production?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>